v 3
d addlogo. Stamp a logo onto a Stata graph.
d
d Stata cannot place a raster image inside the plot region, so addlogo
d exports the current (or named) graph and composites a logo onto it,
d sized relative to the graph width so it looks the same at any export
d resolution.  It stamps the current graph, a named graph, a saved .gph,
d or an already-exported image; nine positions, opacity, and PNG / TIF /
d JPG / PDF output.
d
d The compositing is done by ImageMagick (the "magick" CLI) or by a
d Python + Pillow helper -- whichever is present (engine(auto)).
d
d   addlogo [using image] , logo(file) saving(file) [position() scale() ...]
d
d Requires: Stata 16+, plus one image engine --
d   ImageMagick        (brew install imagemagick), or
d   Python 3 + Pillow  (pip install Pillow).
d
d KW: graph
d KW: logo
d KW: image
d KW: branding
d KW: watermark
d KW: export
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d Distribution-Date: 20260718
d
f addlogo.ado
f addlogo.sthlp
f addlogo_helper.py
